WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.126 --> 00:00:04.415
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:04.415 --> 00:00:05.654
Today, we're going to talk about

00:00:05.654 --> 00:00:08.223
how you can build your courage!

00:00:08.223 --> 00:00:09.674
Rule number five is my personal favorite,

00:00:09.674 --> 00:00:11.723
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:11.723 --> 00:00:13.385
And also, as people are talking,

00:00:13.385 --> 00:00:15.952
if someone says somethin' that
really resonates with you,

00:00:15.952 --> 00:00:16.921
you know the drill!

00:00:16.921 --> 00:00:18.262
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:19.113
put your quotes around it,

00:00:19.113 --> 00:00:21.211
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:21.211 --> 00:00:22.044
Enjoy!

00:00:22.044 --> 00:00:24.544
(light music)

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.071
- [Don] Here's the stats from your show,

00:00:42.071 --> 00:00:44.669
and it says that the richest
85 people on this planet

00:00:44.669 --> 00:00:47.940
have as much money as
the poorest 3.5 billion.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.965
- [Morgan] Yeah, right.

00:00:49.965 --> 00:00:51.882
On the planet, however.

00:00:53.009 --> 00:00:54.378
That's...

00:00:54.378 --> 00:00:56.125
- [Don] That's not far
off, but in America.

00:00:56.125 --> 00:00:58.006
- No, it isn't far off, in America.

00:00:58.006 --> 00:01:01.589
But, we still hear,
don't abandon the idea,

00:01:03.625 --> 00:01:05.927
that it isn't finite.

00:01:05.927 --> 00:01:09.166
It isn't finite, if you were
born, where were you born?

00:01:09.166 --> 00:01:09.999
- [Don] Me?

00:01:09.999 --> 00:01:10.832
- Yeah, you!

00:01:10.832 --> 00:01:11.665
- [Don] Baton Rouge, Louisiana.

00:01:11.665 --> 00:01:12.498
Baton Rouge General Hospital.

00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:14.804
- [Morgan] Baton Rouge, Louisiana!

00:01:14.804 --> 00:01:17.554
I was born in Memphis, Tennessee.

00:01:19.081 --> 00:01:23.248
I had a long haul, from
where I came from, to here.

00:01:25.262 --> 00:01:26.954
But, here we are.

00:01:26.954 --> 00:01:27.787
- [Don] Right.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.402
- So, proof is in, the
proof of the pudding,

00:01:30.402 --> 00:01:31.235
it's in the eating.

00:01:31.235 --> 00:01:32.895
And here, we sit at the dining table.

00:01:32.895 --> 00:01:35.095
- [Don] But, it's hard to, when
you say that to some people,

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.514
because they say, oh, there you go,

00:01:36.514 --> 00:01:39.251
with the pull yourself up
by the bootstraps thing!

00:01:39.251 --> 00:01:41.643
And, you know, you're
just being respectable!

00:01:41.643 --> 00:01:43.810
Not everybody can do that!

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.632
- Bull(beep).

00:01:46.632 --> 00:01:47.799
Everybody can.

00:01:49.752 --> 00:01:51.891
Everybody doesn't...

00:01:51.891 --> 00:01:52.724
Courage.

00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:56.489
Courage is the key, to life itself.

00:01:57.452 --> 00:01:59.669
There are a lot of people
who are born in a situation,

00:01:59.669 --> 00:02:02.151
with, I'll never get out of this.

00:02:02.151 --> 00:02:03.401
So, they won't.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:05.881
I say, to people, who say,

00:02:05.881 --> 00:02:09.030
well, I would like to have
done so, and so, and so.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.290
So, when have you could have done it?

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.690
Say, well, I couldn't get out of here.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.571
Man, the bus runs every day!

00:02:14.571 --> 00:02:18.154
(Don and Morgan chuckling)

00:02:19.017 --> 00:02:20.474
- You're exactly right.
- Yeah!

00:02:20.474 --> 00:02:24.445
- You would say, if you can
conceive it in your mind...

00:02:24.445 --> 00:02:25.803
- [Morgan] If you can
think of it, you can do it.

00:02:25.803 --> 00:02:26.894
That's the human condition!

00:02:26.894 --> 00:02:28.679
If we can imagine it, we can do it!

00:02:28.679 --> 00:02:29.512
- [Don] Right.

00:02:29.512 --> 00:02:32.539
- And I think, that's
the condition of each,

00:02:32.539 --> 00:02:34.327
individual human.

00:02:34.327 --> 00:02:36.827
(light music)

00:02:38.629 --> 00:02:39.688
- Ten years from now,
you're going to arrive.

00:02:39.688 --> 00:02:40.829
The question's where!

00:02:40.829 --> 00:02:41.909
And if you don't do somethin' today,

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:42.768
you're going to show up somewhere!

00:02:42.768 --> 00:02:43.859
So, what happens is,

00:02:43.859 --> 00:02:45.438
when you go through
natural disappointments,

00:02:45.438 --> 00:02:46.518
and frustrations,

00:02:46.518 --> 00:02:48.726
when things don't work
out the way you expected,

00:02:48.726 --> 00:02:52.128
when people betray you, or
disappoint you, or hurt you,

00:02:52.128 --> 00:02:55.837
what happens is, all cynicism
is, all skepticism is,

00:02:55.837 --> 00:02:57.518
is a protective device, that says,

00:02:57.518 --> 00:02:58.351
I don't want to get my hopes up,

00:02:58.351 --> 00:03:00.197
'cause I don't want to feel
that drop of disappointment.

00:03:00.197 --> 00:03:01.146
I don't want to feel the loss.

00:03:01.146 --> 00:03:02.406
I don't want to feel the hurt.

00:03:02.406 --> 00:03:04.376
So, when people tell me, I'm
cynical, I'm pessimistic,

00:03:04.376 --> 00:03:05.685
I look at 'em, and say, listen.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.706
Let's be honest, you're gutless.

00:03:07.706 --> 00:03:10.196
It doesn't take any, any courage,

00:03:10.196 --> 00:03:11.746
to think things don't
work, and they're wrong,

00:03:11.746 --> 00:03:12.907
and they're terrible, and never fixed,

00:03:12.907 --> 00:03:13.905
'cause you'll never be disappointed,

00:03:13.905 --> 00:03:15.856
'cause you'll never take any
actions, so it won't change!

00:03:15.856 --> 00:03:17.112
It's self-fulfilling.

00:03:17.112 --> 00:03:19.214
But, it takes guts, to say,

00:03:19.214 --> 00:03:21.161
I'm going to believe in
something, and try it,

00:03:21.161 --> 00:03:24.313
even though I might fail the
first, fourth, tenth time,

00:03:24.313 --> 00:03:25.279
I'm going to keep going!

00:03:25.279 --> 00:03:26.847
And I believe that most human beings,

00:03:26.847 --> 00:03:28.609
that they put themself on the line,

00:03:28.609 --> 00:03:30.307
they would uncover who they really are.

00:03:30.307 --> 00:03:32.576
But, most of us are so afraid of failing,

00:03:32.576 --> 00:03:35.597
or not looking good, or losing out,

00:03:35.597 --> 00:03:37.757
that we just never discover who we are!

00:03:37.757 --> 00:03:38.718
What I think we have in common,

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.848
is we're willing to step
into the uncertainty.

00:03:40.848 --> 00:03:44.877
All passion is found in
the realm of uncertainty!

00:03:44.877 --> 00:03:46.857
And yet, human beings
are pulled to certainty,

00:03:46.857 --> 00:03:49.603
because we don't want
to deal with our fears!

00:03:49.603 --> 00:03:51.985
Freedom, liberation, as we
break through the fears.

00:03:51.985 --> 00:03:53.395
All of my brethren out there,

00:03:53.395 --> 00:03:55.561
all my brothers and sisters
watching, who are entrepreneurs,

00:03:55.561 --> 00:03:58.161
or are considering being entrepreneurs...

00:03:58.161 --> 00:04:00.173
You are what I'm made for!

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:03.382
I've built 18 companies,
12 I actively manage,

00:04:03.382 --> 00:04:05.664
five billion in savings, and
as I told ya, 12,000 employees!

00:04:05.664 --> 00:04:06.535
It blows my mind!

00:04:06.535 --> 00:04:08.212
I have no business background!

00:04:08.212 --> 00:04:10.122
But, I have this passion, that says,

00:04:10.122 --> 00:04:12.328
I must do more for
others, than anybody else.

00:04:12.328 --> 00:04:14.816
And I will never stop growing,
and I'll never stop changing,

00:04:14.816 --> 00:04:15.945
and I'll never stop improving,

00:04:15.945 --> 00:04:19.486
and I feel alive, by
doing that, as opposed to,

00:04:19.486 --> 00:04:22.296
let me do the same thing, every
day, because I'm good at it.

00:04:22.296 --> 00:04:23.936
And let me continue to do that.

00:04:23.936 --> 00:04:25.837
Hopefully, my life is really good.

00:04:25.837 --> 00:04:29.897
That'll make you feel
numb, if not depressed,

00:04:29.897 --> 00:04:30.916
or frustrated, or overwhelmed,

00:04:30.916 --> 00:04:32.688
which is where most human beings lives.

00:04:32.688 --> 00:04:34.062
- Develop the courage!

00:04:34.062 --> 00:04:35.902
Courage is not the absence of fear.

00:04:35.902 --> 00:04:38.703
Courage is the willingness
to act, in spite of the fear.

00:04:38.703 --> 00:04:40.561
I had a fear of speaking,

00:04:40.561 --> 00:04:42.851
because I don't have a college education.

00:04:42.851 --> 00:04:44.984
I had a fear of becoming an entrepreneur,

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.578
because I never had any experience,

00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:48.249
or any background in business.

00:04:48.249 --> 00:04:50.449
I had a fear of so many things,

00:04:50.449 --> 00:04:53.697
I was living a fear-driven life.

00:04:53.697 --> 00:04:55.807
As you look at yourself,
and look at your goals,

00:04:55.807 --> 00:04:57.889
develop the courage,
to go after your goals,

00:04:57.889 --> 00:05:01.279
to live your dreams, and not
your fears, and understand.

00:05:01.279 --> 00:05:03.168
And here's something
that's very important.

00:05:03.168 --> 00:05:06.468
That anything that's worth
doing, is worth doing badly.

00:05:06.468 --> 00:05:07.748
I didn't want to make any mistakes.

00:05:07.748 --> 00:05:11.058
Hey, anything that's worth doing, at all,

00:05:11.058 --> 00:05:12.958
is worth doing badly, why?

00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:16.879
Because, it's worth doing
right, if you know how to do it.

00:05:16.879 --> 00:05:19.756
But, if you don't know how to
do it, it's worth doing badly,

00:05:19.756 --> 00:05:21.231
until you get it right.

00:05:21.231 --> 00:05:23.979
Just like I messed up, right now! (laughs)

00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:25.549
But, you'll forgive me, won't you?

00:05:25.549 --> 00:05:26.679
Of course, you will!

00:05:26.679 --> 00:05:27.979
So, as you look at yourself,

00:05:27.979 --> 00:05:30.878
anything that's worth
doing, is worth doing badly,

00:05:30.878 --> 00:05:32.240
until you get it right.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.432
And as you make mistakes,
you learn from your mistakes,

00:05:34.432 --> 00:05:36.486
and you come back again,
and again, and again.

00:05:36.486 --> 00:05:39.824
They asked Benjamin Franklin,
no, it was Thomas Edison,

00:05:39.824 --> 00:05:40.657
Thomas Edison!

00:05:40.657 --> 00:05:43.626
They said, Thomas Edison,
how did you continue to,

00:05:43.626 --> 00:05:45.986
to learn how to develop the light bulb,

00:05:45.986 --> 00:05:48.829
in spite of the fact, that
you had 10,000 failures?

00:05:48.829 --> 00:05:51.326
And he said, he didn't
have 10,000 failures.

00:05:51.326 --> 00:05:55.235
He said, he had 10,000
ways that did not work.

00:05:55.235 --> 00:05:56.217
Wow!

00:05:56.217 --> 00:05:57.737
Think about that today!

00:05:57.737 --> 00:06:00.161
- Anything that you're
going through right now,

00:06:00.161 --> 00:06:02.441
if you want to take a big, scary leap,

00:06:02.441 --> 00:06:04.853
and you want to start a
new career, or perhaps,

00:06:04.853 --> 00:06:05.822
start a business.

00:06:05.822 --> 00:06:07.793
Anything that you might
consider a failure,

00:06:07.793 --> 00:06:11.641
is really just a necessary step
on your journey to success.

00:06:11.641 --> 00:06:14.022
So, no matter what
you're facing right now,

00:06:14.022 --> 00:06:16.056
no matter what's getting you so scared,

00:06:16.056 --> 00:06:19.539
there's only one question, that
you need to ask, and answer,

00:06:19.539 --> 00:06:21.576
to find the courage to make that big leap,

00:06:21.576 --> 00:06:23.518
and the question is this.

00:06:23.518 --> 00:06:26.336
What's the worst thing that can happen?

00:06:26.336 --> 00:06:27.747
So, not just by saying, yes,

00:06:27.747 --> 00:06:30.838
but what's the worst thing that
can happen, if you said no?

00:06:30.838 --> 00:06:32.916
So, for example, a few years ago,

00:06:32.916 --> 00:06:34.789
I asked my really dear friend, Laura,

00:06:34.789 --> 00:06:37.137
to come speak at one of our live events.

00:06:37.137 --> 00:06:39.459
Now, this was a big opportunity for her.

00:06:39.459 --> 00:06:41.647
But, I know that it was kind
of stressful, and I said,

00:06:41.647 --> 00:06:43.577
you know what, this is big.

00:06:43.577 --> 00:06:45.397
So, take a few days, think about it,

00:06:45.397 --> 00:06:47.589
because once you say yes,
you're going to be locked in.

00:06:47.589 --> 00:06:49.556
So first, she had to ask herself, well,

00:06:49.556 --> 00:06:53.016
what's the worst thing that
could happen, if I said yes?

00:06:53.016 --> 00:06:55.216
So, for her, it was the stress.

00:06:55.216 --> 00:06:57.520
It was wishing that she never committed,

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.077
which she wished she never committed.

00:06:59.077 --> 00:07:00.258
But, it was also this fear,

00:07:00.258 --> 00:07:03.546
that she was going to
completely freeze up on stage,

00:07:03.546 --> 00:07:05.395
that she was going to mess up horribly,

00:07:05.395 --> 00:07:08.945
and completely ruin her
reputation, which she did not.

00:07:08.945 --> 00:07:10.875
Now, on the flip side,
she had to ask herself,

00:07:10.875 --> 00:07:14.567
what's the worst thing that
could happen, if she said no.

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:15.400
So, you got to get,

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.798
that Laura really wanted
to grow her business,

00:07:17.798 --> 00:07:18.866
and her brand.

00:07:18.866 --> 00:07:21.565
And if she said no to this opportunity,

00:07:21.565 --> 00:07:24.427
she'd have to face herself in
the mirror, every single day,

00:07:24.427 --> 00:07:26.206
and say, nice going, bonehead,

00:07:26.206 --> 00:07:28.345
you had the perfect opportunity
to grow your business,

00:07:28.345 --> 00:07:30.325
and you turned it down!

00:07:30.325 --> 00:07:32.014
So now, it's your turn!

00:07:32.014 --> 00:07:33.265
I want you to ask yourself,

00:07:33.265 --> 00:07:36.844
what's the worst possible
thing, that could happen,

00:07:36.844 --> 00:07:40.344
if you said yes, and you'd fail miserably?

00:07:41.243 --> 00:07:43.075
So, don't just think about this loosely.

00:07:43.075 --> 00:07:44.666
I want you to get really specific,

00:07:44.666 --> 00:07:47.537
and tease out every single scenario,

00:07:47.537 --> 00:07:49.261
that could possibly go wrong,

00:07:49.261 --> 00:07:52.492
and how you deal with it, if it did.

00:07:52.492 --> 00:07:53.931
What most of us discover,

00:07:53.931 --> 00:07:56.572
is that no matter what the
worst case scenario is,

00:07:56.572 --> 00:07:58.337
we can actually handle it.

00:07:58.337 --> 00:08:01.466
But, don't forget, you got
to go on the flip side too,

00:08:01.466 --> 00:08:02.528
and ask yourself,

00:08:02.528 --> 00:08:04.406
what's the worst thing that can happen,

00:08:04.406 --> 00:08:06.763
if you decide to do nothing,

00:08:06.763 --> 00:08:10.074
and keep your life exactly as it is.

00:08:10.074 --> 00:08:13.395
Are your regrets going to start
to pile up, like pancakes?

00:08:13.395 --> 00:08:15.322
Are you going to turn into some miserable,

00:08:15.322 --> 00:08:17.334
self-loathing sad sack?

00:08:17.334 --> 00:08:19.403
I really want you to tease this one out,

00:08:19.403 --> 00:08:21.632
and get all the scenarios on the table,

00:08:21.632 --> 00:08:22.793
and then take a look!

00:08:22.793 --> 00:08:23.861
What do ya got?

00:08:23.861 --> 00:08:26.018
What's the worst of the worst?

00:08:26.018 --> 00:08:28.757
Goin' for it, or not going for it?

00:08:28.757 --> 00:08:32.609
- I believe the master emotion,
of all life, is enthusiasm.

00:08:32.609 --> 00:08:34.609
If you're enthusiastic about somethin',

00:08:34.609 --> 00:08:36.168
you're engaged with it.

00:08:36.168 --> 00:08:37.889
If you're enthusiastic about somethin',

00:08:37.889 --> 00:08:39.108
you feel energized for it.

00:08:39.108 --> 00:08:40.649
If you're enthusiastic about somethin',

00:08:40.649 --> 00:08:43.778
you look forward to waking up
tomorrow, and goin' for it.

00:08:43.778 --> 00:08:46.817
So, prime that feeling every day.

00:08:46.817 --> 00:08:48.889
The way that I do that, is
every morning, in the shower,

00:08:48.889 --> 00:08:49.937
when I'm gettin' ready,

00:08:49.937 --> 00:08:53.037
I think, what can I be
excited about, for today?

00:08:53.037 --> 00:08:54.909
What can I have enthusiasm for, today?

00:08:54.909 --> 00:08:56.708
And if I can't come up with
anything off the top of my head,

00:08:56.708 --> 00:08:59.779
or by looking at my schedule, I create it.

00:08:59.779 --> 00:09:02.888
I say, okay, what could I
do today, that would be fun,

00:09:02.888 --> 00:09:04.687
and make me look forward to the day?

00:09:04.687 --> 00:09:06.173
Maybe, it's prank a friend.

00:09:06.173 --> 00:09:08.626
(chuckles) Maybe, it's do
something good for somebody.

00:09:08.626 --> 00:09:10.373
Maybe it's some thing I'm going to do,

00:09:10.373 --> 00:09:11.473
that I just really enjoy,

00:09:11.473 --> 00:09:13.604
that I won't spend a lot
of time, during the day,

00:09:13.604 --> 00:09:15.345
but I'm going to give
myself thirty minutes,

00:09:15.345 --> 00:09:18.486
doing a passion, small little
project, I'm interested in.

00:09:18.486 --> 00:09:20.744
Whatever it is, prime enthusiasm,

00:09:20.744 --> 00:09:23.182
because if you have that
feeling of enthusiasm,

00:09:23.182 --> 00:09:26.519
that's what going to keep you
passionate over the long term.

00:09:26.519 --> 00:09:28.242
And, please listen.

00:09:28.242 --> 00:09:31.256
You need to prime your
enthusiasms every day.

00:09:31.256 --> 00:09:33.866
See, a lot of people are
very passionate people,

00:09:33.866 --> 00:09:35.814
but they're not living passionately,

00:09:35.814 --> 00:09:39.251
because every day they're not
engaging with what they want.

00:09:39.251 --> 00:09:41.141
You know, they set the
big goal, at New Year's,

00:09:41.141 --> 00:09:43.039
but then, February and April rolls around,

00:09:43.039 --> 00:09:44.159
they've forgotten about it.

00:09:44.159 --> 00:09:47.660
But, the reason that they
were so excited, in January,

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.870
that the New Year, why
is everyone excited?

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:51.452
They're priming enthusiasm.

00:09:51.452 --> 00:09:52.872
They're looking at their goals.

00:09:52.872 --> 00:09:54.802
They're having an emotional connection,

00:09:54.802 --> 00:09:57.773
and commitment to that, and
that excites them for the year.

00:09:57.773 --> 00:10:00.740
So, what you need to do, is
look at your goals every day.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.139
What you need to do is, every day,

00:10:02.139 --> 00:10:03.860
write the things down,
that are important to it,

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:06.789
get excited about doing
that, implementing that,

00:10:06.789 --> 00:10:09.870
experiencing it, and go for it.

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:10.703
- [Gary] It breaks my heart,

00:10:10.703 --> 00:10:13.274
my friends live for Friday night.

00:10:13.274 --> 00:10:14.107
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:10:14.107 --> 00:10:14.940
They really get to the week like,

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:16.334
Monday morning's the worst!

00:10:16.334 --> 00:10:19.103
It's just a huge percentage of one's life,

00:10:19.103 --> 00:10:21.134
I can't wrap my help
around, with the Internet!

00:10:21.134 --> 00:10:23.024
This is not your grandpappy's life!

00:10:23.024 --> 00:10:25.355
We, on the Internet, you
can make sh** happen!

00:10:25.355 --> 00:10:28.102
You can build businesses, or side hustles!

00:10:28.102 --> 00:10:30.936
I just don't understand
why people relegate

00:10:30.936 --> 00:10:33.475
into a losing mentality, and
just thinking they can't.

00:10:33.475 --> 00:10:35.516
You can't, because you want
to be on the bowling team,

00:10:35.516 --> 00:10:36.865
or softball, play video games!

00:10:36.865 --> 00:10:37.951
That's why you can't!

00:10:37.951 --> 00:10:38.784
There's plenty of time!

00:10:38.784 --> 00:10:39.771
Get shit done!

00:10:39.771 --> 00:10:42.368
The level of complaining is unacceptable!

00:10:42.368 --> 00:10:43.636
Look...

00:10:43.636 --> 00:10:44.507
What if I told you,

00:10:44.507 --> 00:10:46.937
this was the last Monday
morning of your life?

00:10:46.937 --> 00:10:48.408
What if I told you, you die this week?

00:10:48.408 --> 00:10:50.869
Would you complain about your crap job,

00:10:50.869 --> 00:10:52.425
or that test you don't want to take?

00:10:52.425 --> 00:10:53.304
I doubt it!

00:10:53.304 --> 00:10:55.905
You can go much higher level thinking!

00:10:55.905 --> 00:10:57.345
Well, that's really what it takes!

00:10:57.345 --> 00:11:00.546
It takes understanding,
that if you're not pumped,

00:11:00.546 --> 00:11:03.344
right now, if you're begrudging
what you're about to do,

00:11:03.344 --> 00:11:05.025
if you're not looking forward,

00:11:05.025 --> 00:11:07.506
please recognize the
world we're living in!

00:11:07.506 --> 00:11:08.339
We're living in a world,

00:11:08.339 --> 00:11:10.066
where there's so much more opportunity!

00:11:10.066 --> 00:11:12.954
This Internet thing created
way more opportunity,

00:11:12.954 --> 00:11:13.886
for all of us!

00:11:13.886 --> 00:11:14.815
Way more!

00:11:14.815 --> 00:11:16.475
I mean, look, we're
really lucky to be alive!

00:11:16.475 --> 00:11:18.574
Look, your mom and dad could have had sex,

00:11:18.574 --> 00:11:21.319
like three minutes later,
and you wouldn't even exist!

00:11:21.319 --> 00:11:22.407
And you're complaining!

00:11:22.407 --> 00:11:24.979
You could have ended
up being a bus, a tree!

00:11:24.979 --> 00:11:27.090
I just don't get the mentality,

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:30.250
of being head-down sad,
on a Monday morning.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.209
I'm going to make Monday morning my bitch!

00:11:32.209 --> 00:11:34.191
I'm going to make you
Saturday, Monday morning!

00:11:34.191 --> 00:11:35.680
That's what I want to do every morning,

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:37.512
and that's what I want from you!

00:11:37.512 --> 00:11:39.065
Please, take a step back,

00:11:39.065 --> 00:11:42.108
and think about how
awesome it actually is!

00:11:42.108 --> 00:11:44.668
And then, recognize that
you can attack the world,

00:11:44.668 --> 00:11:46.287
in a totally different way,

00:11:46.287 --> 00:11:50.658
'cause you were lucky enough,
to be born during this era!

00:11:50.658 --> 00:11:52.147
- So, my take, on building courage,

00:11:52.147 --> 00:11:53.834
is I think it's like a muscle.

00:11:53.834 --> 00:11:55.514
I think it's something
that you need to develop,

00:11:55.514 --> 00:11:57.595
and constantly push, and train yourself,

00:11:57.595 --> 00:11:59.615
to get stronger, and
stronger, and stronger.

00:11:59.615 --> 00:12:02.225
There will be periods, every single day,

00:12:02.225 --> 00:12:05.034
that you have the opportunity,
to build your courage muscle.

00:12:05.034 --> 00:12:07.586
And what usually happens, for most people,

00:12:07.586 --> 00:12:09.896
is they have this
opportunity in front of them,

00:12:09.896 --> 00:12:12.198
that is scary, that
they've never done before,

00:12:12.198 --> 00:12:13.515
that they're afraid of,

00:12:13.515 --> 00:12:15.908
and they'll justify it
with a practical reason.

00:12:15.908 --> 00:12:18.357
You tell yourself you can't
do it, because of all this,

00:12:18.357 --> 00:12:21.416
and it'll make total sense to
you, and you just shrink down.

00:12:21.416 --> 00:12:25.326
You constantly play the
smaller game, the weaker game,

00:12:25.326 --> 00:12:28.127
instead of being bold,
and believing in yourself,

00:12:28.127 --> 00:12:30.437
and trying to go for,
and take that action!

00:12:30.437 --> 00:12:33.247
And so, how do you go from
being afraid, and being scared,

00:12:33.247 --> 00:12:35.516
to actually having the courage to do it,

00:12:35.516 --> 00:12:36.857
here's what I found really helps.

00:12:36.857 --> 00:12:38.607
This has really helped
for me, multiple times,

00:12:38.607 --> 00:12:39.608
and I think it can help you.

00:12:39.608 --> 00:12:41.396
The first part is the awareness.

00:12:41.396 --> 00:12:45.387
So many people just
play small, by default.

00:12:45.387 --> 00:12:48.209
They don't even realize
that they're playing small!

00:12:48.209 --> 00:12:50.086
It's just so ingrained in you,

00:12:50.086 --> 00:12:52.748
that it just happens,
constantly, every day!

00:12:52.748 --> 00:12:55.729
You talk yourself down from
things, every single day,

00:12:55.729 --> 00:12:58.051
and it makes perfect, logical sense!

00:12:58.051 --> 00:13:00.518
The reasons why you say
you can't do something,

00:13:00.518 --> 00:13:01.351
are rational.

00:13:01.351 --> 00:13:03.197
That make sense, and so,
you constantly do it.

00:13:03.197 --> 00:13:04.797
But, when you catch yourself,

00:13:04.797 --> 00:13:05.717
it's usually not in the moments.

00:13:05.717 --> 00:13:07.406
It's like the next day, or the next week,

00:13:07.406 --> 00:13:09.876
you catch yourself, to say, you know what,

00:13:09.876 --> 00:13:13.797
yesterday, I should have done
that, I should have said yes.

00:13:13.797 --> 00:13:15.318
I was just too afraid.

00:13:15.318 --> 00:13:17.277
(grunts) Why didn't I say yes?

00:13:17.277 --> 00:13:20.067
That self-awareness, that's the start!

00:13:20.067 --> 00:13:21.936
That is the start!

00:13:21.936 --> 00:13:23.103
If you can realize it,

00:13:23.103 --> 00:13:24.893
don't worry about it being a day later,

00:13:24.893 --> 00:13:26.223
or two days later, or a week later.

00:13:26.223 --> 00:13:27.863
If you can realize, at any point,

00:13:27.863 --> 00:13:30.263
that you played small the other day,

00:13:30.263 --> 00:13:31.572
that's the starting point!

00:13:31.572 --> 00:13:34.103
Because, the next time it happens,
you want to catch it again,

00:13:34.103 --> 00:13:35.534
it's going to get a little closer.

00:13:35.534 --> 00:13:37.423
Instead of it being the next
day, it'll be a couple hours.

00:13:37.423 --> 00:13:39.690
Next time it happens, it'll
get a little bit closer!

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:40.523
Next time it happens,

00:13:40.523 --> 00:13:42.540
it'll be as you're leaving that meeting!

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.250
You realize, almost instantly,

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:45.922
that (exclaims) I did it
again, I did it again!

00:13:45.922 --> 00:13:46.851
I'm playing small!

00:13:46.851 --> 00:13:48.911
I'm justifying these
things, when I shouldn't be!

00:13:48.911 --> 00:13:49.831
I should better myself!

00:13:49.831 --> 00:13:51.021
I need to believe in myself!

00:13:51.021 --> 00:13:53.750
And then, the magical moment happens!

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:56.400
The magical moment happens,

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.739
when you have the opportunity,

00:13:58.739 --> 00:14:01.131
sitting immediately in front of you,

00:14:01.131 --> 00:14:02.669
and you have the decision to make.

00:14:02.669 --> 00:14:04.550
You catch it, in the moment!

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.689
Instead of the next day, or the next week,

00:14:06.689 --> 00:14:08.660
you catch it, as it's happening,

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:10.512
where somebody asks you
the question, and say,

00:14:10.512 --> 00:14:12.334
do you want to do this?

00:14:12.334 --> 00:14:13.167
And in your head,

00:14:13.167 --> 00:14:14.912
you're thinking about all
the reasons why you can't,

00:14:14.912 --> 00:14:16.540
and you catch yourself!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:17.481
Say, this is it!

00:14:17.481 --> 00:14:18.941
This is what always happens!

00:14:18.941 --> 00:14:20.662
I'm about to play small, again!

00:14:20.662 --> 00:14:25.460
And then, developing the courage
to say, I'm going to do it.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:26.293
I'm going to try.

00:14:26.293 --> 00:14:27.589
I'm going to say yes.

00:14:27.589 --> 00:14:29.212
And what really helped me,

00:14:29.212 --> 00:14:33.784
is just thinking that I am
tired of living with regret.

00:14:33.784 --> 00:14:35.214
Once you can catch it,

00:14:35.214 --> 00:14:37.124
once you have the self-awareness to catch,

00:14:37.124 --> 00:14:39.403
that you're playing small, consistently,

00:14:39.403 --> 00:14:42.343
I was tired of living with the regret

00:14:42.343 --> 00:14:45.762
of constantly playing
smaller than I should.

00:14:45.762 --> 00:14:46.993
And when you're in that moment,

00:14:46.993 --> 00:14:49.344
and you have to make that
decision, and you're afraid,

00:14:49.344 --> 00:14:50.464
it's okay to be afraid!

00:14:50.464 --> 00:14:51.663
It's not be fearless!

00:14:51.663 --> 00:14:52.963
You're going to be afraid!

00:14:52.963 --> 00:14:55.874
It's feeling the fear, doing it anyway,

00:14:55.874 --> 00:14:58.455
because you don't want to live in regret,

00:14:58.455 --> 00:15:00.664
for the rest of your life,
looking back on this moment,

00:15:00.664 --> 00:15:02.640
and saying, I played small, again.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.432
And so, that has really,
really, really helped me a lot.

00:15:05.432 --> 00:15:07.200
It's helped me develop the courage muscle,

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:10.372
to the point now, where whenever
I'm afraid of something,

00:15:10.372 --> 00:15:12.720
whenever I'm worried about
somebody else's opinion,

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:15.469
whenever I feel like,
maybe I can't do that,

00:15:15.469 --> 00:15:18.827
then I have to force
myself, to go out and do it.

00:15:18.827 --> 00:15:21.068
If there's a real reason
not to do it, right,

00:15:21.068 --> 00:15:22.339
like, I'm not interested in it.

00:15:22.339 --> 00:15:23.578
I don't have the passion for that.

00:15:23.578 --> 00:15:25.259
I don't actually care about that.

00:15:25.259 --> 00:15:26.127
Then, I won't go and do it.

00:15:26.127 --> 00:15:27.708
But, if I have a passion for it,

00:15:27.708 --> 00:15:29.743
and then the only reason,
that I'm not doing it,

00:15:29.743 --> 00:15:30.860
is because I'm afraid?

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:33.366
Then, I force myself, to go out and do it.

00:15:33.366 --> 00:15:35.315
And every time you do that,

00:15:35.315 --> 00:15:36.644
you build your courage muscle up.

00:15:36.644 --> 00:15:39.545
Every time you're afraid,
even of one small,

00:15:39.545 --> 00:15:42.159
little interaction, talking
to that girl in the street,

00:15:42.159 --> 00:15:44.637
having that difficult
conversation with your partner,

00:15:44.637 --> 00:15:46.199
or employee, or customer,

00:15:46.199 --> 00:15:48.898
every time you think of
something that you need to do,

00:15:48.898 --> 00:15:51.249
and you're afraid to do
it, and then you do it,

00:15:51.249 --> 00:15:53.507
you build your courage
muscle up, every single time.

00:15:53.507 --> 00:15:55.571
You get stronger, and
stronger, and stronger.

00:15:55.571 --> 00:15:57.411
And what I want you to develop the habit,

00:15:57.411 --> 00:15:58.560
this is so important,

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.371
I want you to develop the habit,

00:16:00.371 --> 00:16:02.429
of whatever something difficult comes up,

00:16:02.429 --> 00:16:06.780
you resolve it, you jump
into it, you address it,

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.231
instead of shrinking down.

00:16:08.231 --> 00:16:09.889
'Cause if shrinking down
is all the way up here,

00:16:09.889 --> 00:16:11.131
and addressing it's all the way down here,

00:16:11.131 --> 00:16:13.717
I want you to start to switch this.

00:16:13.717 --> 00:16:16.288
I want you to switch it.

00:16:16.288 --> 00:16:18.076
Where now, every time
that something major,

00:16:18.076 --> 00:16:19.887
some big problem,
something you're afraid of,

00:16:19.887 --> 00:16:20.918
something that you might regret,

00:16:20.918 --> 00:16:23.277
you're going to attack
it, every single time!

00:16:23.277 --> 00:16:26.438
And you're no longer going
to accept playing small,

00:16:26.438 --> 00:16:28.749
with your business, and with your life.

00:16:28.749 --> 00:16:30.148
So, thank you guys so much for watching!

00:16:30.148 --> 00:16:33.599
I made this video, because
Wombat Philosophy asked me to.

00:16:33.599 --> 00:16:34.777
So, if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover,

